WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.267
-You're a stud.
Yeah, number one.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.300
Not too shabby, huh?
Congrats.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.234
You wear number one
pretty well, bud.

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:07.868
Yeah.
-Thank you. Thanks. Yeah.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:08.934
It's nice.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.067
My first New York --

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:11.501
It's my first
number one anything.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:12.567
-Is it really?
-Yeah.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:13.767
-Before we talk
about "The Watcher,"

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.934
we had your fantastic spouse,
Rose Byrne...

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.467
-Yeah, yeah.
-...on the show two nights ago.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.968
And she was saying how
into Halloween the family was.

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.300
-Oh. It's October, right?
Yeah.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.534
We've been at it since July.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.033
Oh, is that right?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:28.601
My kids are just like -- They
wear costumes almost every day.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.868
So Halloween is like
an affirmation for them

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.167
that, "This is what we should be
doing all the time."

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.467
-Yeah, just wearing costumes
all the time.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.767
What is everyone going as again?

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:38.367
-This year, we're going as Hulk.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:40.100
-Rose is Wonder Woman.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.033
Rocco is Darth Vader.

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:48.467
And the other one is --
Rafael is Jafar.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.868
-Jafar?
-Jafar from --

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.968
You know, the villain
from "Aladdin."

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.234
-Yeah, exactly.
-With the parrot

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.701
and the beard and the thing,
yeah.

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.567
-I love it.
I love it. That's so --

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:57.868
-We love it.
We love it.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.467
That's -- it really is --
it's their favorite holiday.

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:02.567
And, you know, we -- you know,
we do the pumpkin patches.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:05.667
We do the corn mazes
and the cannons.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.434
And, you know, we go through,
like, four versions --

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.100
four pumpkins that rot

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.200
because we've been putting them
out there since August,

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.868
you know, just getting ready.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.334
-So you already had
four rotten pumpkins.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.067
Now, finally,
this is the weekend.

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.367
-This is finally happening,
so we're really excited.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.667
You were telling me backstage,
by the way,

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.334
that you just finished a movie
with Robert De Niro.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.501
-Yeah.
-I worked with De Niro before.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.434
Is it -- It's just amazing
to be next to that guy.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:30.000
-It is. It is.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.901
But I don't, like --
I don't notice it

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.868
when I'm doing it with him,
when I'm acting with him.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:36.334
I mean, I'm very aware that I'm
working with a very good actor

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.534
when we're doing it,

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.767
but I don't really --
I don't really take it --

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.400
-That it's Robert De Niro?
-I don't make it a big deal

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.801
in my head, and it's not,

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:46.033
but it hits me every time,
like, later, when I'm at home.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.300
Like, this last time,

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.033
I worked with him
all day one day in a car,

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.467
and we were like,
"We've got to do a fight

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.734
in the middle of the street."

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:55.200
"You know...you," you know,
screaming at each other,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.367
and then, like,
a big dramatic scene.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.100
And I kept it together all day.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.934
And then I was taking out
the garbage that night

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.167
and literally, like,
had to stop --

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:04.400
it all hit me
like a ton of bricks.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.400
I had to sit down.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.267
I was a little emotional
about it.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.133
I was like, "I can't believe
the day I just had,"

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.100
like, you know,
if the 10-year-old me

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.801
could see
what was happening that day.

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:15.133
-I mean, Robert De Niro.
He's a legend.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.167
-Yeah, he's pretty great.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.167
-I mean,
you're pretty great, too,

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.434
but I mean, you guys together.

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:21.033
But I mean, I love that
that's what made you --

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.434
You're just taking out the trash
and you're like,

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.100
"Wait. Hold on a second."
-Oh.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.634
-"I had the most amazing day."
-I had to sit down.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.334
Like, I was putting
the trash out.

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:28.701
-And go -- and get emotional
and go, "Wow,

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.267
I can't believe
I was just acting..."

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:31.734
-Yeah, I was outside
for a long time.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.167
-..."with one of the greatest
actors of all time."

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.300
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.033
Robert De Niro.
-Yeah, you gotta, right?

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.100
You have to, at some point,
you know, really take it in.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.400
-Take it in.
-I can't do it

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.534
while I'm acting with him
or else, you know, I'm dead.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:42.901
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.267
He won't respect you, yeah.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:45.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah, no, no, no.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.434
He's the greatest.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.067
-Let's talk
about "The Watcher."

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.434
Congrats on this.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:50.534
-Thank you.
-As I said, number one.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.968
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:55.934
-Number one drama series
on Netflix for a while now.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.234
-Ryan Murphy.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.334
-Dude, is it Ryan Murphy?

00:02:58.334 --> 00:02:59.601
-Ryan Murphy knows what's up.

00:02:59.601 --> 00:03:02.033
-Did you have any idea
it would be this big?

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.367
-No.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.033
I mean, no, you can't predict
these things at all.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.434
I mean, I've been in things
that I thought

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.934
were going to do better
commercially, and they weren't.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.701
And you just --
you just never know.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.934
You only can tell -- Like, I've
been doing this a long time.

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.200
I could tell if something's big

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.100
by how I'm treated,
like, at the gym.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.834
You know what I mean?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:21.000
Everybody wants to spot me,
you know what I mean?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.234
Like --
-They all know you there.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:23.467
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.367
Like, they'll always look --
the eye contact.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.234
And the like -- you know,
people don't bother me too much.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:29.567
But, like, now, you know,
they're just there.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:31.334
Like, "That ending, bro."

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:33.033
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:36.601
-Or they want like --
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.200
-"That ending, bro.
I don't know.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.501
We've got to talk about that."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:40.801
People -- People will come
right up to you

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.067
and tell you
what they thought of the ending.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:43.701
-But do you know the story
and hear about the story,

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:46.300
and were you spooked when
you heard even about the story?

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.400
-You know what?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.267
I think that story's
really cool.

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.868
And, you know,
it's just that one story

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:51.934
in "New York Magazine."

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.367
-Yes.
-Is the source of this.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:56.000
And it's been read
so many times.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.934
So, I think, like --
there's something about it --

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.834
I think it's really about fear
and about powerlessness.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.267
And, like, I think the actual
event, to me,

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.133
isn't that interesting.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.634
They never found out who did it,

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.634
but yet,
people are obsessed with it.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.000
I think they're obsessed
with it

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.534
because that feeling
of powerlessness, of being --

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.033
having something
taken away from you

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.834
and not knowing
who's doing it is frightening.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.000
-It's frightening.
-It's terrifying.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.033
-What would you do
in that situation?

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.133
-I was interested in that.

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:21.200
-Would you ever be
in that situation?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.400
-I would never be
in that situation.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.701
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.701 --> 00:04:25.534
-Well, first of all,
I would never live in, like --

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:26.834
I just wouldn't live like that.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.100
I need a lot of people
around me.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.801
I can't live out --
-You mean, like, in a house?

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:33.667
-Yeah. Like, in a house
with a big property.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.334
I like to have --
I like sharing walls.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.667
I do.
I like having --

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:38.667
-Such a New Yorker.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.234
-I believe in
safety in numbers.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:42.367
I like having a lot of people.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.067
-A lot of people around.
-Yeah, I do.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.367
-Yeah, witnesses.
-City person.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.234
-Yeah, they know
exactly what happened.

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:49.601
-Yeah.
-For people that haven't seen

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:50.934
"The Watcher" yet,
can you set up

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:52.868
for everybody what it's about
and who you play?

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.234
-I play -- I play a guy that
runs around the house a lot.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:58.200
[ Laughter ]
I play -- I play a guy who --

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.400
his family, they move in.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.000
They -- you know,
they buy their dream home.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.501
-Aww, that's so cute.
-They -- they put --

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.167
they spend all their money that
they've got from this house.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.634
And the moment they move in,

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:08.667
somebody starts sending creepy,
horrible letters to them.

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:10.501
And -- And they're sort of --

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:13.567
And then I do a lot of running
around the house looking scared.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:15.868
-Yeah, getting letters from
someone called "The Watcher,"

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:16.968
and they're saying,
"I'm watching you."

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:18.033
-Yeah.
-"Just letting you know.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:19.200
Welcome to the neighborhood."

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.701
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.133
[ Laughter ]
-What?!

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.400
-"We noticed -- We noticed
that you've got young blood."

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.601
I have two children in --
in this thing.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:29.100
They refer to them
as "young blood."

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.701
-Oof.

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:31.801
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.868
Here's Bobby Cannavale
in "The Watcher."

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:35.234
Take a look at this.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:38.033
-I am pleased
to know your names now

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:42.167
and the names of the young blood
you have brought me.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:44.934
You certainly
say their names often.

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.634
Ellie, Carter.

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:50.634
Ellie is a lovely pianist
with delicate fingers.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:53.467
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:54.901
[ Door opens ]

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:59.067
657 Boulevard
is happy you're here.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:01.634
♪♪

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:03.167
It's been years
since young blood

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:05.234
ruled the hallways
of the house.

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:08.100
Have you found all
the secrets it holds in it?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.868
Will the young blood
play in the basement,

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:13.701
or are they too afraid
to go down there alone?

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:16.300
I would be very afraid,
if I were them.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.167
It is far away
from the rest of the house.

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:22.100
If you were upstairs, you would
never hear them scream.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.167
-What's going on?

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:25.200
-"What is going on?"

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.534 --> 00:06:28.801
Bobby Cannavale, everybody.

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:31.634
"The Watcher" is on Netflix
right now.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:32.667
Congrats, buddy.
-Thanks, buddy.

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:33.801
-Couldn't happen to
a better guy.

